Update on 10 July 2026: All zipped files are re-uploaded; they should be fine to extract.
Some codes are also re-uploaded to remove the "hard-coded" links.
I use another laptop (MacBook Air M1) for testing and successfully run the four main figures and reproduce the results.

Here are the instructions to construct the four main figures for "Current policies and historical trends constrain future mass loss from the Greenland Ice Sheet" by Siew et al. 2026
Let me know if there is any problem (peter.siew@vuw.ac.nz)

# Step 1: 
- Unzip all the files and put the unzipped folders in the folder that contains the "codes" folder
- Keep the existing file and directory format

# Step 2: 
- You need the following Python packages: numpy, scipy, sklearn, xarray, matplotlib, statsmodels, ipdb, catropy, cftime

# To run the main figures (revised manuscript), you need to have the following in the folder "codes". 
# All the "hard-coded' paths are fixed if you put them in the correct folders
Figure 1 ==> fig1_figS1_take_one_out_validation_autoregress.py
Figures 2 & 3 ==> fig2_fig3_GMT_SLR_fractional_idealized.py 
Figures 4 ==> fig4_new_damped_stable_overshoot.py 
supporting script ==> tools_greenland.py 
supporting script ==> functions_read_gmt_training_data_seperate.py

# These are the codes for supplementary figures (revised manuscript). 
# Some codes overlap with the scripts for the main figures and the scripts in the "create_scripts"
# The "hard-coded" paths still exist. So you need to fix them first before running.
Figures S1 & S2 ==> fig1_figS1_take_one_out_validation_autoregress.py
Figure S3 ==> fig2_fig3_GMT_SLR_fractional_idealized.py
Figure S4 ==> fig4_new_damped_stable_overshoot.py 
Figure S5 ==> realistic_CO2eq_versus_CATS.py --> Figure S5
Figures S6 & S7 ==> SLR2100_versus_GMT_trends_ISMIP6_emulations_GCM.py &
plot_boxplots_CMIP5_and_6_ISMIP6_versus_emulations.py &
use_emulator_to_predict_ISMIP6_save_Y_predict.py
Figure S8 ==> GMT_versus_Greenland_ice_ocean_forcings.py
Figures S9 & S10 ==> plot_sle_timeseries_PISM_four_simulations_ISMIP6.py
Figure S11 ==> /create_scripts/create_obs_constrain_weight.py
Figure S12 ==> /create_scripts/create_save_parameters.py
Figure S13 ==> plot_posteria_model_multiple_histogram.py

# Scripts inside the folder /codes/create_scritps are used to create the necessary files 
# You don't need to run them if you can unzip all ".zip" files :
create_GMT_global_and_Greenland_from_spatial_BEST_ERA5.py --> Create GMT for BEST
create_GMT_global_from_timeseries.py --> Create GMT for CMIP5 and CMIP6
create_damped_stable_overshoot_GMT_from_2100to2300.py --> Create the damped trends, stabilized, overshoot GMTs
create_obs_constrain_weight.py --> Create the parameter weights by history calibration
create_save_parameters.py --> Define the parameter range and create the 1,000 member by Latin hypercube sampling.
create_CATs_Nov2025_new.py --> Extract GMT from the xls file provided by Climate Action Tracker (Climate Analytics)








